{{fbdoc item="title" value="__FB_RISCV32__"}}----
Intrinsic define set for 32-bit RISC-V targets.

{{fbdoc item="syntax"}}
	""__FB_RISCV32__""

{{fbdoc item="desc"}}
	Define without a value created at compile time when the target CPU family is 32-bit RISC-V.  The current use is the experimental ##nuttx-riscv32## target.  This define identifies the CPU family; use ##[[KeyPgDdfbnuttx|__FB_NUTTX__]]## when code depends on NuttX.

{{fbdoc item="ex"}}
%%(freebasic)
#ifdef __FB_RISCV32__
	print "32-bit RISC-V target"
#endif
%%

{{fbdoc item="ver"}}
	- Since fbc 1.20.2

{{fbdoc item="see"}}
	- ##[[KeyPgDdfbriscv64|__FB_RISCV64__]]##
	- ##[[KeyPgDdfbnuttx|__FB_NUTTX__]]##
	- ##[[CompilerOpttarget|Compiler Option: -target]]##

